// The intelligent driver model of examples/traffic/idm.ent against the
// same model in plain C (examples/traffic/check/idm.c): two ring roads,
// 52 cars, 6,000 steps of 0.1 s, every car's place and speed every 100
// steps and what the roads measured, to the bit, on one core and on all.
// RUN: clang -O2 -ffp-contract=off %S/../../examples/traffic/check/idm.c -lm -o %t.c
// RUN: %t.c > %t.want
// RUN: %ent run -I %S/../../examples/traffic %S/Inputs/traffic_idm.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.one
// RUN: %ent run --parallel -I %S/../../examples/traffic %S/Inputs/traffic_idm.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.all
// RUN: cmp %t.want %t.one
// RUN: cmp %t.want %t.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.one

// Sugiyama's road has its jam: its cars stopped 189 times in the 300 s
// measured.
// CHECK: road of 22 cars driven {{[0-9]+}} stops 189
// CHECK: road of 30 cars driven
